1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,400
[gentle waves and birdsong]

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,680
Every evening, the sea asks the same
question.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,420
I put on the coat. I bank the stove. I
answer.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,800
My father rowed this water. His father cut
these steps.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
[soft piano begins]

6
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:27,950
The crossing is short. It only feels like
a life.

7
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:33,470
Halfway out, the sun lets go of the day.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,950
And the water holds the last of it, the
way I hold his name.

9
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:48,950
The tower waits. It has never once waited
badly.

10
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,500
[oars creak against the swell]

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,650
One match. One wick. One turn of the
little wheel.

12
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:59,220
And the light goes out across the water —
so nobody else has to ask.

13
00:00:58,200 --> 00:00:59,400
[the beam sweeps the water]

